      "description": "Its title alludes to the new 625-line broadcasting technology, which provided higher image quality. Jazz 625 captured the excitement of the newly launched BBC2 and showcased the cream of American – and occasionally British – musicians during their UK tours. This talk sheds light on the history of jazz on television through a close examination of Jazz 625, accompanied by rare excerpts from its episodes, featuring jazz giants such as Duke Ellington , Coleman Hawkins , Thelonious Monk , Erroll Garner , Ben Webster , Bill Evans , and many more.",
      "color": "#1565c0",
